      "content": "One serious hidden issue is **internal checking or seasoning stresses** that develop over time, even in seemingly sound wood. Improperly treated or installed beams can also suffer from **creep**, where the load causes the wood to slowly deform permanently under sustained weight. Finally, ensure the beam's connection at the supports is robust, as failure here can be an internal load transfer issue rather than the wood failing itself.",
      "source": "target",
